cook time: 2 hours 15 minutes
author: Laure Joliet
time required: 2 hours 35 minutes
prep time: 20 minutes
source: https://www.thekitchn.com/one-pot-recipe-easy-french-ratatouille-recipes-from-the-kitchn-106669
cuisine: Europe, French
---

Heat @olive oil{2%tbsp} in a large #Dutch oven{} or heavy-bottomed pot over medium-high heat until shimmering. 

Add @eggplant{1 1/2%lbs}(large dice), season generously with @kosher salt{} and @freshly ground black pepper{}, and cook, stirring occasionally, until browned in spots, about 2 minutes. Transfer to a large bowl.

Add @olive oil{2%tbsp} to the pot. Add @zucchini or summer squash{1 1/2%lbs}(large dice), season generously with @kosher salt{} and @freshly ground black pepper{}, and cook, stirring occasionally, until browned in spots, about 2 minutes. Transfer to the bowl with the eggplant.

Reduce the heat to medium. Add the remaining @olive oil{1%tbsp} and @yellow onion{1}(diced), season with @kosher salt{} and @freshly ground black pepper{}, and cook, stirring occasionally, until softened and just beginning to brown, ~{6-8%minutes}. 

Add @garlic{2%cloves}(minced), @fresh thyme{2%sprigs}, and @bay leaf{1} and cook until fragrant, about ~{30%seconds}. 

Add @tomatoes{1%lbs}(large dice) and @bell pepper{1%large}(dice). Add the reserved eggplant and zucchini and gently stir to combine. 

Bring to a simmer, then turn down the heat to medium-low. Simmer, stirring occasionally, for at least ~{20%minutes} or up to ~{90%minutes}. A shorter cooking time will leave the vegetables in larger, more distinct pieces; longer cooking times will break the vegetables down into a silky stew.

Remove the @bay leaf{} and @fresh thyme{}.

Just before serving, stir in @basil leaves{1/4%cup}(thinly sliced). Taste and season with @kosher salt{} and @freshly ground black pepper{} as needed. Serve, sprinkling each serving with more @basil leaves{} and drizzling with more @olive oil{}.

> Making a larger batch: This recipe can be doubled and adapted to use whatever vegetables you have. Flavor extras: For something different, try adding a tablespoon of smoked paprika, a pinch of red pepper flakes, 1/4 cup of red wine, or a splash of vinegar to the ratatouille. Storage: Leftovers can be refrigerated in an airtight container for up to 5 days.